  "label": "User projected onto the meme's accusatory text",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material of the meme, specifically the accusatory phrase 'notice how the kenyan skidmark has been silent about the mueller report?'. This text implicitly addresses the viewer, inviting them to notice and judge Obama's silence, thereby projecting the user's role as an observer and accuser. The deictic 'notice' functions as an implicit 'you' or 'the viewer', directing the user to engage with the meme's hateful message and to project their own judgment onto the scene.",
